  "notes": "An A&R-producer-arranger, and the lane's string-and-vocal-arrangement specialist, 1990–2010. The research is candid that his tempo \"follows the record he is dressing (55–105) — he is an arranger over other people's beds as often as a track producer\", so that band is used as written with the mode at 73 and `halfTime` true, because his one fully-sourced record is a 73 BPM D-minor ballad with the backbeat on 3. The drum deltas therefore encode what he *adds* rather than what he programs: \"he generally does not program — on 'Be Without You' the drum bed is Cox's; Fair adds live percussion and the arrangement layer around it\", marked `[LOW-CONF]`. So the kick, snare and hat are the sparse Cox-school bed the entry attributes to that record — one or two kicks, a clap on beat 3, a 0.13 hat lane — while the percussion is the delta: five lanes (tambourine, shaker, conga, triangle, snap) at three to seven hits a bar and −4 dB, the densest percussion of any ballad model in this section, with `quantizeStrength` at 0.6 and `velocityVar` 0.26 because it is played. The identifying parameter is the countermelody, and the research says so outright: \"**string and vocal arrangements are the parameter**… expect a string section entering at the bridge, unison-to-divisi writing, and a stacked background choir on the out-chorus\". So `countermelody.densityRatio` is 0.68 — the highest in this section — with three styles alive, and the chord voicing spans thirty-six semitones for the divisi. \"His structural signature is the **orchestral lift** — verse and first chorus kept dry, strings and choir introduced at bridge/final chorus\" is the arrangement. The bass \"adds double bass / low strings under an existing 808 or synth-bass part, doubling roots an octave down\", also `[LOW-CONF]`, so the register floor is MIDI 22 — the lowest here — at a 0.96 root follow. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED, and this model is the section's clearest case of encoding an arranger's layer rather than a programmer's grid. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"whatever the track dictates\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
